🔹 Process
Definition: An independent program in execution.

Memory: Has its own memory and resources.

Isolation: Processes are isolated from each other.

Creation: More resource-intensive (takes more time and memory).

Communication: Needs Inter-Process Communication (IPC) like sockets, files.

Crash Impact: One process crash does not affect others.

Example: Running Chrome and Word are two separate processes.

🔸 Thread
Definition: A smaller unit of a process, used for multitasking within a process.

Memory: Shares memory with other threads in the same process.

Isolation: Not isolated; can affect each other.

Creation: Lightweight and faster to create.

Communication: Easier (since memory is shared).

Crash Impact: If one thread crashes, it can affect the whole process.

Example: In Chrome, one tab is a thread within the browser process.

🔁 Summary Table:
| Feature       | Process                 | Thread                           |
| ------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------- |
| Memory        | Own memory              | Shared memory with other threads |
| Creation      | Slow and resource-heavy | Fast and lightweight             |
| Communication | Complex (IPC)           | Easy (shared memory)             |
| Isolation     | Fully isolated          | Not isolated                     |
| Crash Impact  | Safer                   | Risk of process crash            |
| Use Case      | Running different apps  | Doing multiple tasks in one app  |
